    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0486" n="390" xml:id="pg390"/>

                <head>No. 203.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Quito,
                                Ecuador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 25,
                        1873</date>. (Received November 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I forward Nos. 1 and 2, copy and
                    translation, of a decree just issued by the President of the republic, whereby
                    those persons accused of political offenses, now expatriated from Ecuador, are
                    granted the privilege of return upon proper application, &amp;c., to the
                    minister of the interior.</p>
                <p>I am much gratified to be able to forward this document to the Department, as it
                    betokens a spirit so entirely at variance with that which generally controls the
                    governments of the Spanish American republics.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RUMSEY WING.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d205-a1.xml" xpointer="d205-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
